15:24.540 --> 15:26.580
So it's going to be called customers.

15:26.580 --> 15:29.660
And then below we're going to have something called table schema.

15:29.660 --> 15:33.180
It is just like a logical thing that's going to group up my tables.

15:33.180 --> 15:35.100
And as a default we have the DBO.

15:35.140 --> 15:38.540
But of course we can go and create our own schema if you want.

15:38.580 --> 15:40.500
I'm just going to leave it now as a default.

15:40.500 --> 15:42.140
So let's go and hit next.

15:42.180 --> 15:46.860
Now skill going to show you like a preview of the data just to make sure that everything is correct.

15:46.860 --> 15:48.100
So it looks nice.

15:48.100 --> 15:49.700
So let's go and click next.

15:49.740 --> 15:54.780
Now we're going to get like a metadata or let's say description for the structure of our table.

15:54.780 --> 15:58.580
So we have the column name the data type primary keys and allow nulls.

15:58.580 --> 16:02.580
And of course you can go and rename your columns over here or change the data type.

16:02.580 --> 16:05.630
I'm just going gonna leave everything as a default because it is correct.

16:05.630 --> 16:06.710
Then go next.

16:06.750 --> 16:08.790
We have here a summary about the imports.

16:08.790 --> 16:09.990
So I'm going to say finish.

16:09.990 --> 16:11.670
And as you can see it is successful.

16:11.670 --> 16:12.710
So let's close it.

16:12.750 --> 16:15.550
Of course I'm not seeing anything in the object explorer.

16:15.590 --> 16:17.710
Let's go and refresh the database.

16:17.710 --> 16:19.350
So over here refresh.

16:19.350 --> 16:20.950
And then go again to the tables.

16:20.950 --> 16:23.270
And you can see now our new table the customers.

16:23.270 --> 16:26.670
So right click on it and say select top 1000 rows.

16:26.670 --> 16:30.750
And with that we have our first table inside our new database.

16:30.790 --> 16:32.990
And of course we have done this for only one table.

16:32.990 --> 16:36.270
In order to get all other tables we have to repeat the process again.

16:36.270 --> 16:39.750
So right click on the sales db, then new one the two.

16:39.790 --> 16:43.430
And then we're going to go to the task and the same thing import flat file.

16:43.430 --> 16:47.110
So you go through the five files in order to get the whole database.

16:47.110 --> 16:49.910
So this is a second way on how to create a database.

16:49.910 --> 16:54.510
But now we have a third way on how to do it by restoring a backup file.

16:54.510 --> 16:55.590
So how are we going to do it.

16:55.630 --> 16:58.990
We're going to go again to the object explorer over here to the databases.

16:58.990 --> 16:59.990
Right click on it.

16:59.990 --> 17:02.190
And this time we will not create a new database.

17:02.190 --> 17:04.480
We're going to say we want to restore it.

17:04.600 --> 17:06.200
So restore database.

17:06.240 --> 17:10.520
Now we're going to get a window in order to help you restoring the database for the sources we're going

17:10.520 --> 17:11.520
to say device.

17:11.520 --> 17:14.200
And then we're going to go over here to those three dot points.

17:14.200 --> 17:15.120
So click on it.

17:15.160 --> 17:16.440
You're going to get a second window.

17:16.440 --> 17:18.400
You're going to say add over here.

17:18.400 --> 17:19.520
So click on that.

17:19.560 --> 17:23.520
And now we're going to see the locations where the server is storing the backups.

17:23.520 --> 17:25.480
So you can see we don't have anything yet.

17:25.480 --> 17:28.840
But we're going to put our backups exactly in this location.

17:28.840 --> 17:34.040
So what you have to do first to go and copy the whole path over here and then go open this folder.

17:34.040 --> 17:35.200
So now I am over here.

17:35.240 --> 17:40.000
It of course depends where you install the SQL server and the version of the Express Edition.

17:40.000 --> 17:41.400
So we don't have anything yet.

17:41.400 --> 17:47.400
But if you go to the course materials and then go to datasets, then SQL server, you're going to find

17:47.400 --> 17:51.160
those two backup files, the my database and the sales DB.

17:51.200 --> 17:57.240
So we have to copy them and go to the backup and just paste everything over here so that we have now

17:57.240 --> 18:00.080
the backup files inside the database folder.

18:00.120 --> 18:02.480
And now we have to go and just restore them.

18:02.480 --> 18:04.170
Let's go back to the clients.

18:04.210 --> 18:05.650
Now, of course, we don't see anything.

18:05.650 --> 18:07.090
We have to refresh first.

18:07.090 --> 18:09.570
And now, as you can see, we are able to see the backups.

18:09.610 --> 18:14.610
Now let's go and pick, for example, the sales DB and then hit okay and then another.

18:14.610 --> 18:15.090
Okay.

18:15.130 --> 18:19.690
Now before we start restoring I'm gonna put another location for the database.

18:19.690 --> 18:22.050
So I'm going to say it is database three.

18:22.090 --> 18:26.650
Since I have everything already with that it's going to go and create a new database for it.

18:26.650 --> 18:29.730
So everything is ready for the restore and just hit okay.

18:29.770 --> 18:30.610
Now look at this.

18:30.650 --> 18:33.370
It says database is restored successfully.

18:33.410 --> 18:36.450
Let's just click okay over here and you can see it on the left side.

18:36.450 --> 18:37.890
If not then just refresh.

18:37.890 --> 18:40.050
So let's go inside it to the tables.

18:40.050 --> 18:42.370
You're gonna find exactly the same data.

18:42.370 --> 18:46.570
So of course if you want the other database, you just have to do and repeat the same steps.

18:46.570 --> 18:51.290
And with that I showed you the three different ways on how to create databases in SQL server.

18:51.330 --> 18:54.850
The first one and the easiest one is just running the SQL scripts.

18:54.850 --> 18:55.330
Another one.

18:55.330 --> 18:59.050
You have to create a brand new database and import files to it.

18:59.050 --> 19:03.900
And a third option, if you have the backup files, then you just go and restore the database.

19:03.900 --> 19:07.340
So those are the three options and I hope the first option already worked for you.

19:07.380 --> 19:08.500
Now about the third option.

19:08.500 --> 19:12.300
It is one way on how we communicate databases between each others.

19:12.300 --> 19:16.900
So if I have a nice database, I can just go and create a backup and send it to you.

19:16.900 --> 19:19.260
And then from your side you can go and restore it.

19:19.260 --> 19:23.700
And now if you want to get other databases that you want to practice, you can search for example for

19:23.740 --> 19:25.700
download Adventureworks.

19:26.260 --> 19:32.580
So if you search for this and then you go to the Microsoft link, you can find in the Microsoft documentations

19:32.900 --> 19:34.820
you have here a lot of backup files.

19:34.820 --> 19:37.180
So here you have like different types of databases.

19:37.180 --> 19:38.700
The first one called OLTP.

19:38.780 --> 19:41.300
It is very similar to real life applications.

19:41.300 --> 19:45.660
It is transactional system where the data is not yet prepared for analysis.

19:45.660 --> 19:51.340
But if you want something that is easy to analyze, then you have to go and get the data warehouse is

19:51.340 --> 19:56.820
perfectly prepared for you to do analytics, and as well you can use it in order to connect it to power

19:56.820 --> 19:57.300
BI.

19:57.300 --> 19:58.980
And a third type called lightweight.

19:58.980 --> 20:04.140
If you want just few tables so you can download this backup file, put it in the database and restore

20:04.180 --> 20:04.500
it.
